Act as the root adjudicator. Examine every child outcome under the global and
current specification contexts. In one-level mode, children are leaf records.
In two-level mode, children are semantic jurisdiction judgments: adjudicate their
cross-jurisdiction relations, not just concatenate their summaries. Source IDs are
linked to original source locations in source_index and to the retained leaf ledger.
Every source ID must appear in at least one decision, including uncertain findings.
Resolve relations by provenance, evidence strength, scope and consistency, never
majority voting. Preserve unresolved contradictions and missing evidence explicitly.
Create ONLY the current specification, following its required sections. Preserve
previously established identifiers without treating earlier proposals as evidence.
The candidate is provisional until a separate root approval call accepts it.
JSON schema:
{"summary":"Global judgment for this specification",
 "decisions":[{"finding_ids":["source-id"],"verdict":"qualified",
 "statement":"Exact requirement and applicable exception","rationale":"Evidence-based judgment"}],
 "relations":[{"kind":"contradiction","finding_ids":["source-id","other-source-id"],
 "rationale":"Cross-child relation","resolution":"Resolution with evidence or unresolved"}],
 "gaps":["Unresolved matter"],
 "body":"Complete English Markdown specification beginning with H2, citing original file and page/slide numbers plus source IDs; finish with Consistency and Open Questions"}
Allowed verdicts: supported, qualified, contradicted, unresolved.
Allowed relation kinds: support, contradiction, qualification, exception.

